# Illegal: a function that declares a return type has to hand one back on every
# path, and all three of these reach the closing brace without returning - an
# `if` with no else, an `if` whose else falls through, and a CONDITIONAL loop,
# whose body may not run at all.
#
# Refused at typecheck rather than in codegen, so each one carries the location
# of the function it is about and all three are reported at once.
#
# `loopOnly` is the case the loop rule has to tell apart from a legal
# `while (true) { ... }`, which never reaches the statement after it and is
# accepted.
